// Selection.select answers with the SETTLED published selection plus whether the request actually moved it.
// `selected` exists because "the element resolves but cannot be located on screen" is a NORMAL outcome, not an
// error: a collapsed branch, a zero-size element, a control scrolled out of a virtualized list, or an element
// whose visual is not realized yet all produce it. Reporting that as a fault made every such tree row click a
// red error in a client, while reporting it as success made the client believe a selection landed that never
// did -- and the very next Selection.poll disagreed. `selected:false` therefore carries the UNCHANGED prior
// generation/handle, so a client reconciles to the truth instead of guessing.
WINAPP_DEVTOOLS_PROTOCOL_TYPE(SelectionSelectResult, R"devtools({"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["selected","generation","handle"],"properties":{"selected":{"type":"boolean"},"generation":{"type":"integer"},"handle":{"type":"string"}}})devtools")
